        "rationale": "The workspace should share graph-space interaction semantics. Reflow during render makes focus, return, and zoom appear to move graphs and creates a second layout authority.",
        "status": "decided",
        "decidedAt": "2026-10-18T20:28:38.047Z",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "supersededBy": "",
        "body": "Treat each graph instance offset as authored workspace geometry. Insert and explicit Tidy may choose positions. Drag updates the offset. Focus, zoom, semantic presentation, and ordinary render passes may change the camera or compact frame, but they must not mutate the offset or create a transient placement override. Keep legacy placement flags only as a compatibility boundary until later cleanup.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-graph-space-unification"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1784322332554,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Gavel"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/decision.node-class.node"
      }
    },
